.TH GGE 1 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
gge \- generalGameEngine project tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gge
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gge
scaffolds and documents games built on generalGameEngine. It lives in the
engine repository at
.I tools/gge
and is normally run from a game's root as
.IR vendored/engine/tools/gge .
Every command accepts
.B \-h
for its own option list.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "init [\-o " DIR "] [\-e " URL "] [\-I] [\-T] " name
Create a new game project: CMakeLists.txt, src/main.c, src/game_state.h,
src/scenes.h, a title and a game scene, an assets/ tree, gge.conf, and the
engine as a git submodule at vendored/engine.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Parent directory to create the project under (default .).
.TP
.BI \-e " URL"
Engine repository to add as the submodule (default: this engine's origin).
.TP
.B \-I
Enable SDL_image (PNG loading).
.TP
.B \-T
Enable SDL_ttf (TrueType fonts).
.RE
.TP
.BI "scene [\-o " DIR "] [\-t " TYPE "] [\-H " HEADER "] [\-n] [\-f] " name
Write
.IR src/scenes/scene_ name .c
from the scene template and declare
.IB name _scene()
in src/scenes.h.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Output directory (default src/scenes).
.TP
.BI \-t " TYPE"
Sets the two stack flags: \fBfull\fR (blocks update and render below; title,
gameplay), \fBoverlay\fR (blocks update, shows below; pause, dialog; the
default), or \fBhud\fR (blocks nothing).
.TP
.BI \-H " HEADER"
Header that receives the declaration (default src/scenes.h).
.TP
.B \-n
Do not touch the header.
.TP
.B \-f
Overwrite the file if it exists.
.RE
.TP
.BI "entity [\-o " DIR "] [\-H] [\-f] " name
Write
.IR src/entities/ name .h
and
.IR .c :
a pointer-free struct, init/tick functions, and a hitbox helper.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Output directory (default src/entities).
.TP
.B \-H
Header only, for an all-inline entity.
.TP
.B \-f
Overwrite existing files.
.RE
.TP
.BI "config [\-f " FILE "] [\-e " HEADER "] [" key " [" value ]]
Show, set, or emit project settings. Settings live in
.I gge.conf
as key=value lines and are emitted to
.I src/gge_config.h
as
.BI GGE_ KEY
macros, which main.c uses to fill EngineConfig. Strings are quoted, numbers
are bare.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-f " FILE"
Settings file (default gge.conf).
.TP
.BI \-e " HEADER"
Header to generate (default src/gge_config.h).
.RE
.TP
.BI "man [\-s " SECTION "] [\-k] " topic
Open a manual page. Functions, types (structs, enums) and macros are section
3, one page each, named exactly as in the headers (\fBgge man Camera\fR,
\fBgge man engine_push\fR, \fBgge man CUT_DO\fR). Module and concept pages
are section 7 and are opened by their short name (\fBgge man scenes\fR opens
\fBgge\-scenes\fR(7)); \fBgge man overview\fR is the place to start and
\fBgge man api\fR indexes every section\-3 page by module. This page is
section 1.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-s " SECTION"
Force a section: 1 tools, 3 functions/types/macros, 7 modules and concepts.
.TP
.B \-k
Keyword search: list pages mentioning
.I topic
instead of opening one.
.RE
.TP
.BI "ls [\-m " MODULE "] [\-g " REGEX "] [\-t]"
List every public engine function with its module and one-line description.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-m " MODULE"
Only this engine folder (sprite, menu, tilemap, ...).
.TP
.BI \-g " REGEX"
Filter names.
.TP
.B \-t
List types and macros instead of functions.
.RE
.TP
.B genman
Regenerate the section\-3 pages and
.BR gge\-api (7)
from the engine headers. A
.B /** ... */
comment directly above a prototype, a typedef, or a #define becomes that
page's DESCRIPTION;
.B @return
(functions),
.B @field name text
(struct fields and enum values) and
.B @see
lines are honored, and names containing a hyphen in @see refer to section\-7
pages. A prototype without a block uses the trailing comment on its line; a
struct field without an @field line uses its own trailing comment.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I gge.conf
Project settings (title, logical_w, logical_h, window_scale, tick_rate, tile,
org, app).
.TP
.I src/gge_config.h
Generated from gge.conf; do not edit, do not commit.
.TP
.I tools/templates/*.in
Templates with @NAME@, @UPPER@, @TITLE@, @TYPE@ placeholders.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gge init \-I \-T \-o ~/games cat_simulator
gge scene \-t hud minimap
gge scene \-o src/ui \-t overlay shop
gge entity dog
gge config tick_rate 120
gge man engine_push
gge man Camera
gge man scenes
gge man overview
gge ls \-m tilemap
gge ls \-t
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gge\-overview (7),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge\-engine (7),
.BR gge\-scenes (7),
.BR gge\-state (7),
.BR gge\-entities (7),
.BR gge\-input (7),
.BR gge\-drawing (7),
.BR gge\-build (7)
